      <section class="dark-section section-pad" aria-labelledby="project-title">
        <div class="container">
          <span class="mono accent eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> ONGOING R&amp;D / MUJOCO SIMULATION</span>
          <h1 class="project-title" id="project-title">Hybrid Embodied AI for Dual-Arm Manipulation</h1>
          <p class="project-intro">I’m using Python to integrate GRIT manipulation policies with a C++ RMPflow motion executor for the dual-arm Rainbow RB-Y1 in MuJoCo. The project explores how learned policies and model-based control can work together during coordinated manipulation and contact with objects.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="light-section section-pad" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
        <div class="container about-grid">
          <div class="about-left">
            <span class="mono chapter-tag">01 / SYSTEM OVERVIEW</span>
            <h2 id="overview-title">From Human Instructions to Robot Action</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="about-right">
            <p>The architecture is designed to turn a high-level human instruction into a task plan, validate it, and pass it to a motion executor. I’m integrating these stages and testing the RB-Y1 execution layer in MuJoCo.</p>
            <figure class="system-overview-film">
              <iframe src="../animations/system-overview.html?v=3" title="Animated walkthrough from human instructions to simulated robot action" loading="lazy"></iframe>
              <figcaption>Illustrative system flow · MuJoCo integration in progress · No fluid simulation</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="light-section section-pad" aria-labelledby="reasoner-title">
        <div class="container about-grid">
          <div class="about-left">
            <span class="mono chapter-tag">02 / TASK REASONING</span>
            <h2 id="reasoner-title">Reasoner on Mac mini M4</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="about-right">
            <p>I developed the project’s Reasoner on a Mac mini M4. This is the task reasoning layer, where I’m exploring how to use scene context to propose manipulation steps.</p>
            <p>I’m designing the perception pipeline around RGB-D observations, object segmentation, and geometric scene representations. Connecting those inputs to the Reasoner and passing its task plans to the motion executor are integration goals.</p>
