      <section class="dark-section section-pad-tight" aria-labelledby="executor-title">
        <div class="container">
          <span class="mono accent eyebrow">04 / EXECUTOR</span>
          <h2 id="executor-title">Modified GRIT and C++ RMPflow</h2>
          <p class="project-intro">I’m integrating a modified GRIT manipulation policy in Python with a C++ RMPflow motion executor for the dual-arm RB-Y1 in MuJoCo. GRIT provides learned manipulation commands. RMPflow combines motion objectives during execution. I’m testing how the two work together during coordinated grasping and contact.</p>
          <h3>Coordinating the bottle and cup</h3>
          <figure class="project-demo">
            <video controls playsinline preload="none" width="960" height="458" poster="../media/rb-y1-mujoco-poster.jpg" aria-describedby="simulation-caption">
              <source src="../media/rb-y1-mujoco-sequence-2x.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
              <a href="../media/rb-y1-mujoco-sequence-2x.mp4">Download the simulation clip</a>
            </video>
            <figcaption id="simulation-caption" class="demo-footnote">Work in progress in MuJoCo, shown at 2× speed. The simulated RB-Y1 reaches for the cup and bottle, grasps and lifts both, then tilts the bottle toward the cup. No fluid is simulated.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
