            <div class="next-card-body">
              <h2 id="ur10-title">Related work on the UR10</h2>
              <div>
                <p>In a separate study, I evaluated RMPflow-Magnetic on a physical UR10 equipped with end-of-arm radar. The C++ reactive policy used radar range and Doppler closing speed to steer around obstacles while preserving motion toward the goal. The experiments included moving transparent obstacles.</p>
                <a class="text-link" href="https://doi.org/10.1109/LRA.2026.3706942">Read the IEEE RA-L paper <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                <p><a class="text-link" href="../#rmpflow-explainer">Watch Why Magnetic Steering Fits RMPflow <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
              </div>
            </div>
